As per recent requirements shared by the Nautilus application development team, they need custom images created for one of their projects. 
Several of the initial testing requirements are already been shared with DevOps team. 
Therefore, create a docker file /opt/docker/Dockerfile (please keep D capital of Dockerfile) on App server 1 in Stratos DC and configure to build an image with the following requirements:

a. Use ubuntu:24.04 as the base image.

b. Install apache2 and configure it to work on 5001 port. (do not update any other Apache configuration settings like document root etc).

SOLUTION
On App Server 1 in Stratos DC, create /opt/docker/Dockerfile with the following content:

bash
sudo mkdir -p /opt/docker
sudo tee /opt/docker/Dockerfile > /dev/null <<'EOF'
FROM ubuntu:24.04

ENV DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive

RUN apt-get update && \
    apt-get install -y apache2 && \
    sed -i 's/^Listen 80$/Listen 5001/' /etc/apache2/ports.conf && \
    sed -i 's/<VirtualHost \*:80>/<VirtualHost *:5001>/' /etc/apache2/sites-available/000-default.conf && \
    rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

EXPOSE 5001

CMD ["apache2ctl", "-D", "FOREGROUND"]
EOF
Verify the file:

bash
cat /opt/docker/Dockerfile
To build the image (replace <image-name>:<tag> as needed):

bash
cd /opt/docker
sudo docker build -t <image-name>:<tag> .
This Dockerfile:

Uses ubuntu:24.04 as the base image.

Installs apache2 using apt.

Changes Apache’s listen port from 80 to 5001 in /etc/apache2/ports.conf.

Updates only the default VirtualHost port from 80 to 5001; it does not change document root or other Apache settings.

Exposes port 5001.

Starts Apache in the foreground so the container stays running.

